      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b96",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 142990338,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 350039454,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783157932572,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hEtpiNIiEOYsEje_p1rF5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 166.1782059601088,
      "y": 6040.83850052091,
      "width": 2278.638671875,
      "height": 70,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b97",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1769070366,
      "version": 11,
      "versionNonce": 995044994,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783157957900,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-  DynamoDB is schema-less, meaning you don't need to define a schema before inserting data. \n   This means items in the same table can have different sets of attributes, and new attributes can be added to items at any point without affecting existing items.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-  DynamoDB is schema-less, meaning you don't need to define a schema before inserting data. \n   This means items in the same table can have different sets of attributes, and new attributes can be added to items at any point without affecting existing items.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "c3x-s49EcgUYAVrHIhHaM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 190.75711949252968,
      "y": 6160.437223557997,
      "width": 2171.734619140625,
      "height": 420,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b98",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1672662878,
      "version": 65,
      "versionNonce": 1077343774,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783158261848,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Tables \nServe as the top-level data structure in DynamoDB, each defined by a mandatory primary key that uniquely identifies its items. \nTables support secondary indexes, enabling queries on non-primary key attributes for more versatile data retrieval.\n\nItems\nCorrespond to rows in a relational database and contain a collection of attributes. Each item must have a primary key and can contain up to 400KB of data, \nincluding all its attributes.\n\nAttributes\nKey-value pairs that constitute the data within an item. \nThey can vary in type, including scalar types (strings, numbers, booleans) and set types (string sets, number sets). Attributes can also be nested, \nallowing for complex data structures within a single item.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Tables \nServe as the top-level data structure in DynamoDB, each defined by a mandatory primary key that uniquely identifies its items. \nTables support secondary indexes, enabling queries on non-primary key attributes for more versatile data retrieval.\n\nItems\nCorrespond to rows in a relational database and contain a collection of attributes. Each item must have a primary key and can contain up to 400KB of data, \nincluding all its attributes.\n\nAttributes\nKey-value pairs that constitute the data within an item. \nThey can vary in type, including scalar types (strings, numbers, booleans) and set types (string sets, number sets). Attributes can also be nested, \nallowing for complex data structures within a single item.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
