      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 207423198,
      "version": 79,
      "versionNonce": 2139015042,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783159025431,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In SQL, you'd write:\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE user_id = 101\n\nBut in DynamoDB, this would be translated to a query\noperation like this:\n\nconst params = {\n  TableName: 'users',\n  KeyConditionExpression: 'user_id = :id',\n  ExpressionAttributeValues: {\n    ':id': 101\n  }\n};\n\ndynamodb.query(params, (err, data) => {\n  if (err) console.error(err);\n  else console.log(data);\n});",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In SQL, you'd write:\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE user_id = 101\n\nBut in DynamoDB, this would be translated to a query operation like this:\n\nconst params = {\n  TableName: 'users',\n  KeyConditionExpression: 'user_id = :id',\n  ExpressionAttributeValues: {\n    ':id': 101\n  }\n};\n\ndynamodb.query(params, (err, data) => {\n  if (err) console.error(err);\n  else console.log(data);\n});",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
