      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- DynamoDB supports two consistency models for read operations: eventual consistency and strong consistency. \n  Importantly, this is not a table-level configuration -- you choose the consistency model on each individual read request \n  by setting ConsistentRead=true",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- DynamoDB supports two consistency models for read operations: eventual consistency and strong consistency. \n  Importantly, this is not a table-level configuration -- you choose the consistency model on each individual read request \n  by setting ConsistentRead=true",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
