      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783159301990,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- DynamoDB scales through auto-sharding and load balancing. When a partition reaches capacity (in size or throughput), \n  DynamoDB automatically splits it and redistributes data. \n- Hash-based partitioning ensures even distribution across nodes, balancing traffic and load.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- DynamoDB scales through auto-sharding and load balancing. When a partition reaches capacity (in size or throughput), \n  DynamoDB automatically splits it and redistributes data. \n- Hash-based partitioning ensures even distribution across nodes, balancing traffic and load.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "zCt2vzH7fAdwyTL2OqRs-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -159.5260651422969,
      "y": 11299.375394615552,
      "width": 775.263671875,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9p",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 107799810,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 420809858,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783159206546,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "DynamoDB automatically replicates your data across\nthree Availability Zones within a region -- this is not\nuser-configurable. Each partition maintains three replicas\n(one leader and two followers) managed entirely by AWS.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "DynamoDB automatically replicates your data across three Availability Zones within a region -- this is not user-configurable. Each partition maintains three replicas (one leader and two followers) managed entirely by AWS.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "s_ne7M67G8jgEp-k-zgql",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 277.580234636339,
      "y": 11503.198758858718,
      "width": 1583.188506987824,
      "height": 70,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 425013470,
      "version": 207,
      "versionNonce": 1910856798,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783159301990,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- DynamoDB automatically replicates your data across three Availability Zones within a region -- this is not user-\nconfigurable. Each partition maintains three replicas (one leader and two followers) managed entirely by AWS.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- DynamoDB automatically replicates your data across three Availability Zones within a region -- this is not user-configurable. Each partition maintains three replicas (one leader and two followers) managed entirely by AWS.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "rNf2KxvfSPzq9Bn0pzksH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 246.77342597292778,
      "y": 11124.30034380105,
      "width": 1771.4240543987928,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 939736606,
      "version": 172,
      "versionNonce": 537929346,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783159297442,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- For strongly consistent reads, DynamoDB routes the request directly to the leader, which always has the most up-to-date\ndata. For eventually consistent reads, any of the three replicas can serve the request, which provides lower latency but might\nreturn slightly stale data.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- For strongly consistent reads, DynamoDB routes the request directly to the leader, which always has the most up-to-date data. For eventually consistent reads, any of the three replicas can serve the request, which provides lower latency but might return slightly stale data.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
